      "id": "e86daafd33fc",
      "title": "The Hounding",
      "author": "Xenobe Purvis",
      "publicationDate": "2025-06-24",
      "pageCount": 240,
      "location": null,
      "lat": null,
      "lng": null,
      "status": "read",
      "notes": "NYT January book club pick. Beautiful descriptive writing. You feel the cracked summer dryness. This is easily translated into the thirst of the villagers for violence. But I think this is ultimately a story about women and power. It's a story about women told primarily through the eyes of men. About women who have no real control over their lives and at the same time too much freedom. I love the open ended ending and the way it shows that whatever was true never mattered. It is only what people believe that matters.",
